  "question": {
    "text": "The remainder left out when $8^{2 n}-(62)^{2 n+1}$ is divided by 9 is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n0\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n2\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n7\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n8",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& 8^{2 n}-(62)^{2 n+1}=(1+63)^n-(63-1)^{2 n+1} \\\\\n& =(1+63)^n+(1-63)^{2 n+1}=\\left(1+{ }^n c_1 63+{ }^n c_2(63)^2+\\ldots .+(63)^n\\right)+\\left(1-{ }^{(2 n+1)} c_1 63+{ }^{(2 n+1)} c_2(63)^2+\\ldots .+(-1)(63)^{(2 n+1)}\\right) \\\\\n& =2+63\\left({ }^n c_1+{ }^n c_2(63)+\\ldots .+(63)^{n-1}-{ }^{(2 n+1)} c_1+{ }^{(2 n+1)} c_2(63)+\\ldots .(63)^{(2 n)}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n$\\therefore$ Reminder is 2"
  }
}